# Flashy 

A desktop flashcard app for learning French vocabulary, built with Python and Tkinter.

## How it works

- Each card shows a French word. After a few seconds, it flips to reveal the English translation.
- Click ✅ if you knew the word — it's removed from your deck and won't show up again this session.
- Click ❌ if you didn't — it stays in the deck so you'll see it again.
- Your progress (the words you still need to learn) is saved to `words_to_learn.csv` as you go.
- Once you've gone through every word, the app shows a "Done" screen.
- Every time you restart the app, you begin fresh with the full word list.

## Running it

Make sure you have `pandas` and `ttkthemes` installed:

```
pip install pandas ttkthemes
```

Then run:

```
python main.py
```

Make sure `data/french_words.csv` and the `images/` folder (card front/back, right/wrong buttons) are in place before launching.
